.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt HALOW-MCS-SUMMARY.PY 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm halow-mcs-summary.py
.Nd summarize a HaLow peer's modulation and coding rates
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -iface Ar interface
.Op Fl -shell
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads
.Li iw dev interface station dump
and selects a peer with transmit or receive MCS data.
The most recently active peer is preferred, with signal strength breaking ties.
Run with permission to query wireless station information.
.Pp
Default output is JSON containing the interface, selected peer MAC,
transmit and receive rate summaries, signal, inactivity and peer count.
The count includes only peers with MCS data.
No usable station data produces empty rate fields and a zero count.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -iface Ar interface
Wireless interface; default
.Li wlan2 .
.It Fl -shell
Print quoted shell assignments instead of JSON.
Variable names start with the uppercased interface name, with punctuation
replaced by underscores, and end in
.Li TX_MCS , RX_MCS , MCS_PEER , MCS_SIGNAL_DBM
or
.Li MCS_PEER_COUNT .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after producing output, including when station data is unavailable.
Invalid arguments return 2.
Empty fields do not establish that the interface is healthy or idle.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo halow-mcs-summary.py --iface wlan2
.Ed
